      why: 'Sampling error falls with the square root of n. Quadrupling n halves the error bar; ten times better precision needs a hundred times the interviews. This is why serious polls cluster around 1,000–2,000 respondents and why the design (randomness, stratification, weighting) matters more than raw size.',
